ion and concludes that none has sufficient substance to justify not doing so. It therefore suggests that there is now an alternative policy approach to the current one for minimising the number and severity of road casualties attributable to speed. It is no longer necessary to rely on improvements in vehicle handling and crash worthiness and on appeals for higher standards of driving -and on the law-abiding instincts of most drivers.(a) for the covering abstract of the seminar see IRRD 812997.","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423490","pdf":"","k":["Law enforcement","Enforcement","Crash","Transport engineering","Politics","Control (management)","Law","Engineering"]},{"doi":"10.1080/01442878708423485","t":"Community and social structure","a":["Peter Willmott"],"d":"1987-07-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423485","pdf":"","k":["Political science","Sociology","Regional science"]},{"doi":"10.1080/01442878708423483","t":"Long distance weekly commuting","a":["Terence Hogarth"],"d":"1987-07-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423483","pdf":"","k":["Geography"]},{"doi":"10.1080/01442878708423482","t":"The social fund — will it work?","a":["Richard Berthoud"],"d":"1987-07-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423482","pdf":"","k":["Work (physics)","Business","Public relations","Political science","Engineering"]},{"doi":"10.1080/01442878708423486","t":"The extent and nature of temporary employment in Great Britain","a":["Bernard H. Casey"],"d":"1987-07-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423486","pdf":"","k":["Political science","Business","Economics"]},{"doi":"10.1080/01442878708423484","t":"What role for the social sciences?","a":["Nigel Forman"],"d":"1987-07-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01442878708423484","pdf":"","k":["Political science","Sociology","Social science","Regional science"]},{"